---
/**
 * Landing (index.astro only): the file behind the demo answer, shown as the
 * plain-markdown note it is. Rendered on the bright "paper" surface from the
 * design tokens, a deliberate contrast block on the dark page. The paper
 * tokens are static (not theme-flipped), so hardcoded accents here are tuned
 * for paper and read the same in both themes. The fiction matches the
 * terminal demo one column over: Boris, the access-platform cutover, the
 * superseded June date. The frontmatter fields (type, status, owner, updated,
 * tags, summary) and the superseded stamp are the real vault contract.
 */
---

<figure class="m-0">
  <div class="note">
    <div class="tab">
      <svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.7" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true">
        <path d="M14 3v5h5"></path>
        <path d="M14 3H6a1 1 0 0 0-1 1v16a1 1 0 0 0 1 1h12a1 1 0 0 0 1-1V8z"></path>
      </svg>
      <span>projects/access-platform.md</span>
    </div>
    <div class="body">
      <p class="fence">---</p>
      <p class="fm"><span class="k">type:</span> project</p>
      <p class="fm"><span class="k">status:</span> active</p>
      <p class="fm"><span class="k">owner:</span> "<span class="link">[[people/boris-carter]]</span>"</p>
      <p class="fm"><span class="k">updated:</span> 2026-06-11</p>
      <p class="fm"><span class="k">tags:</span> [work, access-platform]</p>
      <p class="fm"><span class="k">summary:</span> Cutover moved to July 15, gated on the parallel-run numbers.</p>
      <p class="fence">---</p>

      <p class="h1"># Access platform</p>
      <p class="prose">
        Cutover is <mark>July 15</mark>, gated on the two-week parallel-run numbers.
        <span class="link">[[people/boris-carter]]</span> owns it.
      </p>
      <p class="dead"><s>Cutover is June 20.</s></p>
      <p class="stamp">&gt; superseded by <span class="link">[[events/2026-06-11-boris-1-1]]</span></p>
    </div>
  </div>
</figure>

<style>
  /* the exhibit shell, identical across all four captures on this page: 1rem
     corner, hairline, filled surface, NO shadow. The card used to carry a
     raw-rgba drop shadow and a 1.1rem corner of its own, which made it the one
     exhibit shaped differently from its three siblings - and the shadow was a
     hardcoded warm brown that did nothing on the dark ground. */
  .note {
    overflow: hidden;
    border-radius: 1rem;
    border: 1px solid var(--color-line);
    background: var(--color-surface);
    color: var(--color-ink);
  }
  .tab {
    display: flex;
    align-items: center;
    gap: 0.5rem;
    padding: 0.625rem 1rem;
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: 0.75rem;
    color: var(--color-ink-chrome);
    /* the chrome PLANE, not bg-soft: this card lands on a bg-soft section, so
       the old value made the band the exact colour of the page behind it */
    background: var(--color-chrome);
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--color-line);
  }
  /* the file glyph is chrome, so it takes the chrome ink. In the accent it was
     a decorative use (the accent's semantic jobs are links, the $ marker, the
     path chips, the scores) and it measured 2.8:1 on the band, under the 3:1
     floor a meaningful glyph needs. The band now speaks in one voice. */
  .tab svg {
    width: 0.9rem;
    height: 0.9rem;
    flex: 0 0 auto;
    color: currentColor;
  }
  .body {
    padding: 1.15rem 1.25rem 1.25rem;
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: 0.79rem;
    line-height: 1.7;
    overflow-wrap: break-word;
  }
  .body p {
    margin: 0;
  }
  /* the fence is three thin rules of glyph, so at the faint step it optically
     washes out and the frontmatter looks like it starts on blank space. It
     carries the chrome step, above the key column, so the block reads fenced. */
  .fence {
    color: var(--color-ink-chrome);
  }
  /* a wrapped frontmatter value (or the superseded stamp) has to read as a
     continuation, not as another key, so continuation lines hang in */
  .fm,
  .stamp {
    padding-left: 2ch;
    text-indent: -2ch;
  }
  .k {
    color: var(--color-ink-faint);
  }
  .h1 {
    margin: 0.9rem 0 0.45rem;
    font-size: 0.95rem;
    font-weight: 700;
  }
  .prose {
    margin: 0 0 0.85rem;
  }
  .link {
    color: var(--color-accent);
    text-decoration: underline dotted;
    text-underline-offset: 3px;
  }
  mark {
    background: color-mix(in oklab, var(--color-accent) 15%, transparent);
    color: inherit;
    padding: 0 0.15em;
    border-radius: 3px;
  }
  .dead {
    color: var(--color-ink-faint);
  }
  /* the supersede stamp is a line of the file, not a footnote about it. At
     0.72rem it was the only run in the card set smaller than the file's own
     body, which read as a caption the site had added rather than as markdown
     the contract wrote - and this line is exactly what the paragraph beside
     the card points at. Same size as the body, one step down in ink. */
  .stamp {
    color: var(--color-ink-soft);
  }
</style>
